  "notes": [
    "No gendered past-tense verb agrees with the player or a placeholder: transitive pasts use the ergative એ construction (agreement with the object), otherwise a colon form (તૈયાર: {arg1}) or the honorific plural with તમે.",
    "Plural categories follow Intl.PluralRules(\"gu\"): one covers 0 and 1, other the rest.",
    "Postpositions (નું, માં, ને, એ) attach to placeholders as Gujarati writes them; નું/ની/નો agree with the possessed noun, not the placeholder.",
    "Generated names use the default order (first part, space, second part): Gujarati puts the modifier first (વજ્ર શિખર, કિરમજી કમળ). First parts are invariant adjectives or nouns, so every pair reads naturally; generatedNames can stay unset.",
    "Kagemura and brand names stay in Latin letters; the many \"mostly uses a different script\" warnings come from short strings dominated by these names or technical identifiers.",
    "Japanese statutory pages (tokushoho, shikin-kessai) are translated into Gujarati; the support page links them by their Japanese titles.",
    "This translation has not been reviewed by a native Gujarati speaker."
  ]
